<Base title="About — Tomás Campoy Rojo" description="About Tomás Campoy Rojo, Data Engineer at UCAM focused on cloud data platforms and analytics engineering.">
  <section class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">About</div><h1>Engineering data systems with enough context to make good decisions.</h1><p>I’m a Data Engineer at UCAM, working in the overlap between engineering, analytics and institutional decision systems.</p></section>
  <article class="article">
    <p class="kicker">My default mode is to reduce ambiguity: define the source of truth, make transformations reproducible, expose data quality, and give downstream users a stable contract.</p>
    <h2>Current work</h2>
    <p>At Universidad Católica San Antonio de Murcia (UCAM), I work on data engineering and institutional analytics problems: ingesting and reconciling operational data, automating recurring workflows, building analytical datasets and improving the performance and reliability of internal data processes.</p>
    <p>My work has included survey and response processing, institutional rankings, academic and admissions data, alumni analytics, and data products used by non-technical teams. Where the work is public or can be described safely, I document the engineering lessons in the Work section.</p>
    <h2>Technical focus</h2>
    <p>My core stack is Python, Polars, SQL, Airflow, dbt, Spark and Databricks, with cloud work across AWS, Azure and GCP. I’m especially interested in lakehouse architecture, CDC, streaming, orchestration, data quality and the operational side of data platforms.</p>
    <h2>Certifications</h2>
    <ul><li>AWS Certified Data Engineer – Associate</li><li>Azure Databricks Platform Architect</li></ul>
    <h2>What I optimize for</h2>
    <p>Correctness before cleverness. Explicit trade-offs. Measurable performance. Systems that are easy to inspect when they fail. Documentation that explains why the architecture exists rather than simply listing technologies.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
